// The temperate seas and the south (V2-10 (f)): the warm-temperate shelves of every ocean (the
// sardine's and the mackerel's, upwelling off California, Peru and the Cape), their sea lions,
// fur seals, dolphins and penguins, and the Southern Ocean about Antarctica. Densities are per km²
// of sea; birth days are the north's calendar (the south's come half a year later).
